    Step 6: Verify Freeze Time From Freeze Start


Step 1: Start Syslog
    [Documentation]
    ...  In Step 1 Syslog is started

    Log  \nStep 1: Start Syslog  console=${True}
    ute_syslog.Start Syslog
    ...    alias=${SYSLOG_ALIAS}
    ...    log_dir=${FILE_DIR}
    ...    log_name=${SYSLOG_NAME}
    ...    ip=${LMP_eNB_IP}

Step 2: Collect Snapshot
    [Documentation]
    ...  In Step 2 Snapshot is colleced using WebEM

    Log  \nStep 2: Collect Snapshot  console=${True}
    @{time}=    Get Time    year month day hour min
    Set Test Variable  ${SNAPSHOT_LOCATION}  ${BTSFiles}/snapshot_${time[0]}_${time[1]}_${time[2]}_${time[3]}_${time[4]}
    ${snapshot_status}    Run Keyword And Return Status
    ...    coam.Collect Snapshot   ${SNAPSHOT_LOCATION}.zip    timeout=${SNAPSHOT_TIMEOUT}
    Run Keyword If    '${snapshot_status}' != '${True}'    Run Keywords
    ...    Custom Test Teardown
    ...    AND    verdicts.Set Test Failed  TC failed - Collecting snapshot using WebEM has failed.  ${TRUE}


Step 3: Stop Syslog
    [Documentation]
    ...  In Step 3 Syslog is stopped

    Log  \nStep 3: Stop Syslog  console=${True}
    ute_syslog.Stop Syslog  alias=${SYSLOG_ALIAS}


Step 4: Get Time Freeze Values From Syslog To Csv File
    [Documentation]
    ...  In Step 4 python script is used to generate timetable file from syslog,
    ...  containing information how long it took for snapshot logs to be freezed by BTS/DU/CU.

    Log  \nStep 4: Get Time Freeze Values From Syslog To Csv File  console=${True}
    Run Process  python  Freeze_Files9.py  ${FILE_DIR}/${SYSLOG_NAME}  shell=${True}  cwd=${CURDIR}/tc_variables  timeout=120
    Move File  ${FILE_DIR}/${CSV_FILE_NAME}  ${BTSFiles}


Step 5: Verify Freeze Time From Snapshot Start
    [Documentation]
    ...  In Step 5 records from timetable are verified if snapshot logs were frozen by BTS/DU/CU in allowed time limit
    ...  from the moment the snapshot collection request is received.

    Log  \nStep 5: Verify Freeze Time From Snapshot Start  console=${True}
    ${file_content}    OperatingSystem.Get File    ${BTSFiles}/${CSV_FILE_NAME}
    @{lines} = 	Split To Lines 	${file_content}
    ${line_counter}=    Set Variable  ${0}
    ${list_of_elements}=   Create List
    FOR 	${var} 	IN 	@{lines}
        Run Keyword If 	'${line_counter}' > '${NUMBER_OF_LINE_IN_CSV_FILE_TO_SKIP - 1}'    Add Record To List    ${var}    ${list_of_elements}
	    ${line_counter} =    Set Variable    ${line_counter + 1}
    END
    ${list_of_elements_length} =   Get Length  ${list_of_elements}
    FOR  ${list_item_id}    IN RANGE   ${list_of_elements_length}
        ${checker_if_file_name_is_special}=    Run Keyword And Return Status    Should Contain
        ...    ${list_of_elements}[${list_item_id}][${COLUMN_NUMBER_WITH_FILE_NAME - 1}]    ${FILE_NAME_FOR_EXECPTION}
        ${checker_if_file_name_is_special_2}=    Run Keyword And Return Status    Should Contain
        ...    ${list_of_elements}[${list_item_id}][${COLUMN_NUMBER_WITH_FILE_NAME - 1}]    ${FILE_NAME_FOR_EXECPTION_2}
        ${current_freeze_file_value}=    Set Variable    ${list_of_elements}[${list_item_id}][${COLUMN_NUMBER_WITH_FREEZE_TIME - 1}]
        Run Keyword If    ${checker_if_file_name_is_special}    Run Keywords
        ...    Set Test Variable    ${FREEZE_LIMIT_FOR_EXCEPTIONS}        ${10000}
        ...    AND     Check Freeze Time For Exceptions    ${current_freeze_file_value}
        ...    ELSE IF    ${checker_if_file_name_is_special_2}    Run Keywords
        ...    Set Test Variable    ${FREEZE_LIMIT_FOR_EXCEPTIONS}        ${30000}
        ...    AND     Check Freeze Time For Exceptions    ${current_freeze_file_value}
        ...    ELSE    Check Freeze Time From Snapshot Start    ${current_freeze_file_value}
    END

Step 6: Verify Freeze Time From Freeze Start
    [Documentation]
    ...  In Step 6 records from timetable are verified if log files were frozen by its respective components
    ...  in allowed time limit from the moment the internal components started freezing the log files.

    Log  \nStep 6: Verify Freeze Time From Freeze Start  console=${True}
    ${file_content}    OperatingSystem.Get File    ${BTSFiles}/${CSV_FILE_NAME}
    @{lines} = 	Split To Lines 	${file_content}
    ${line_counter}=    Set Variable  ${0}
    ${list_of_elements}=   Create List
    FOR 	${var} 	IN 	@{lines}
        Run Keyword If 	'${line_counter}' > '${NUMBER_OF_LINE_IN_CSV_FILE_TO_SKIP - 1}'    Add Record To List    ${var}    ${list_of_elements}
	    ${line_counter} =    Set Variable    ${line_counter + 1}
    END
    ${list_of_elements_length} =   Get Length  ${list_of_elements}
    FOR  ${list_item_id}    IN RANGE   ${list_of_elements_length}
        ${checker_if_file_name_is_special}=    Run Keyword And Return Status    Should Contain
        ...    ${list_of_elements}[${list_item_id}][${COLUMN_NUMBER_WITH_FILE_NAME - 1}]    ${FILE_NAME_FOR_EXECPTION}
        ${checker_if_file_name_is_special_2}=    Run Keyword And Return Status    Should Contain
        ...    ${list_of_elements}[${list_item_id}][${COLUMN_NUMBER_WITH_FILE_NAME - 1}]    ${FILE_NAME_FOR_EXECPTION_2}
        ${current_value_from_freeze_start}=    Set Variable    ${list_of_elements}[${list_item_id}][${COLUMN_NUMBER_WITH_FREEZE_TIME - 2}]
        Run Keyword If    ${checker_if_file_name_is_special}    Run Keywords
        ...    Set Test Variable    ${FREEZE_LIMIT_FOR_EXCEPTIONS}        ${10000}
        ...    AND     Check Freeze Time For Exceptions    ${current_value_from_freeze_start}
        ...    ELSE IF    ${checker_if_file_name_is_special_2}    Run Keywords
        ...    Set Test Variable    ${FREEZE_LIMIT_FOR_EXCEPTIONS}        ${30000}
        ...    AND     Check Freeze Time For Exceptions    ${current_value_from_freeze_start}
        ...    ELSE    Check Freeze Time From Freeze Start    ${current_value_from_freeze_start}
    END


Check Freeze Time From Snapshot Start
    [Documentation]
    ...     This keyword verifies if freezing time from start of snapshot is not longer than allowed freezing time.
    [Arguments]  ${time_value}
    Run Keyword If 	${time_value} >= ${FREEZE_LIMIT_FROM_SNAP_START}   verdicts.Set Test Failed
    ...    Time freeze value are not correct. Condition ${time_value} < ${FREEZE_LIMIT_FROM_SNAP_START} is not passed.  ${TRUE}

Check Freeze Time For Exceptions
    [Documentation]
    ...     This keyword verifies if freezing time is not longer than allowed time for exception files.
    [Arguments]  ${time_value}
    Run Keyword If 	${time_value} >= ${FREEZE_LIMIT_FOR_EXCEPTIONS}    verdicts.Set Test Failed
    ...    Time freeze value are not correct. Condition ${time_value} < ${FREEZE_LIMIT_FOR_EXCEPTIONS} is not passed.  ${TRUE}

Check Freeze Time From Freeze Start
    [Documentation]
    ...     This keyword verifies if freezing time from freeze start is not longer than allowed freezing time
    [Arguments]  ${time_value}
    Run Keyword If 	${time_value} >= ${FREEZE_LIMIT_FROM_FREEZE_START}    verdicts.Set Test Failed
    ...    Time freeze value are not correct. Condition ${time_value} < ${FREEZE_LIMIT_FROM_FREEZE_START} is not passed.  ${TRUE}

Add Record To List
    [Documentation]
    ...     This keyword splits strings using separator and add records to list
    [Arguments]    ${record_value}    ${list_of_elements}
        ${record_split} =    Split String    ${record_value}    ${CSV_SEPARATOR}
        Append To List      ${list_of_elements}    ${record_split}

Custom Test Teardown
    ute_syslog.Stop Syslog  alias=${SYSLOG_ALIAS}
    Log    Syslog stopped    console=${True}

TC Setup
    Common Test Setup    syslog_launch=${False}

TC Teardown
    Run Keywords
    ...    interface.Common step trigger
    ...    AND    Setup Scout And Send Configuration
    ...    AND    Common Test Teardown
